  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 211 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nA more robust trough will move east across the northern US from \nSunday into early next week. This will renew the periodic scattered \nthunderstorms chances each day while also helping to squash the\nthermal ridge. We will not see substantial cooling, however \ntemperatures Sunday into early next week should be at least a \nfew degrees cooler than what we have seen this week. The ridge \ndoes look to rebuild for the middle to end of next week. Heat \nand humidity along with continued scattered thunderstorm chances\nlooks to be the story for at least another week.",
